      "reasoning": "thought\n`Tribute to the Wild` cast.\nChoice: `Spell Crumple` or `Troll Ascetic`.\nI am NOT going to counter my own spell.\nI'll let it resolve.\nStoic and Timmy will have to sacrifice something.\nStoic: Likely an artifact (Sol Ring or Mind Stone).\nTimmy: Likely an artifact/enchantment (Sword of Hours or Fertile Ground).\nThis weakens both. Excellent.\n\n\"SITREP! TRIBUTE TO THE WILD IS IN THE AIR! WAIT FOR IMPACT!\"\n\nAction: `choose_action(answer=false)`\nThen wait for resolution.\nThen I'll play `Mulldrifter` or `Sphinx`.\n\nWait, if I have 10 mana left (after 1G for Tribute).\nMulldrifter (5). Left with 5.\nSphinx (5)? Or whatever it costs. Sphinx costs 3UU (5).\nI could play BOTH if I have enough mana.\n12 lands. 2 used for Tribute. 10 left.\n5 + 5 = 10.\nPERFECT.\n\n\"MAGGOTS! WE'RE DEPLOYING EVERYTHING! FLYING SQUADRON, MOVE OUT!\"\n\nAction: `choose_action(answer=false)`\nWait for priority.\n...\nWait, let's call `get_action_choices` after passing.\n...\nWait, should I cast `Spell Crumple` if they try to protect their stuff?\n(They can't really protect from \"Sacrifice\" with a spell unless they counter Tribute).\nIf they counter Tribute, I might counter back?\nActually, keep Crumple for a board wipe or a win-con.\n\"SAVE THE AMMO FOR THE BIG ONES!\"\n\nAction: `choose_action(answer=false)`.",
