      "reasoning": "This is great! It's my turn, and I have several options. I need to look at my hand and what's available carefully.\n\nMy hand still has \"Angelic Gift\", \"Netherese Puzzle-Ward\", and \"Curse of Verbosity\".\nHowever, `get_action_choices` also shows some cards from my graveyard that I can activate or cast somehow: \"Tainted Peak - Play Tainted Peak\", \"Dreamborn Muse - Cast Dreamborn Muse\", \"Fey Steed - Cast Fey Steed\".\nThis is a bit confusing since my game state showed these cards as being in exile or graveyard. I will prioritize actions that get me more value.\nMy current available mana seems decent. I have 6 untapped lands.\nI see \"Sword of Hours\" - Equip {2}. I have Skullbriar, the Walking Grave on my battlefield, but it's tapped. Equipping it now won't allow me to attack with it this turn unless it gets untap.\nI also see \"Lumbering Falls\" can become a creature, but it needs {2}{G}{U}.\n\nLooking at the new choices, it appears I can cast \"Winged Boots\" for {1}{U}. This gives a creature flying and hexproof, which is great.\n\"Angelic Gift\" for {1}{W} gives flying and draws a card. This is also good.\n\"Curse of Verbosity\" for {2}{U} is an enchantment.\n\"Netherese Puzzle-Ward\" for {3}{U} is an artifact.\n\nMy strategy was to get out Holy Avenger and Argentum Armor, but they are in the graveyard. I need to work with what I have.\n\nI have 3 cards in my hand: Angelic Gift, Netherese Puzzle-Ward, Curse of Verbosity.\nAnd some other options from the `get_action_choices` that are not in my hand according to `get_game_state`, but are somehow playable: Tainted Peak, Fey Steed, Dreamborn Muse, Winged Boots. This is probably due to some effects on the battlefield that allow me to play cards from exile or graveyard.\n\nLet's look at the available mana. I have 6 untapped lands.\nI have a \"Skullbriar, the Walking Grave\" with 2 +1/+1 counters on it. It's currently a 3/3 tapped",
