      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "maggots! Scry 3 from Prognostic Sphinx. I need meat, not dirt! Gravedigger is a decent recruit, but I need to clear the way. Let's send the Swamp and Terramorphic Expanse to the bottom! They're just taking up space in my supply line! Gravedigger... maybe you can stay on top for a later mission. \n\nWait, the prompt asks for cards to put on the BOTTOM. I'll put the lands on the bottom.\n\nActually, scry 3 usually means I can keep what I want on top in any order.\nChoices are Gravedigger, Terramorphic Expanse, Swamp.\nLand drop for turn is done? Hard to say without checking main phase info, but it's turn 10. I probably have enough lands.\n\nI'll put both lands on the bottom. index 1 and 2. \nActually, I have to do them one by one.\nBottom: Terramorphic Expanse (1), Swamp (2).\nKeep: Gravedigger (0) on top.\n\nWait, if I want to keep Gravedigger, I just don't select it for the bottom.\nWait, SCry 3. I select cards to put on bottom.\nI'll select Swamp first. Then Terramorphic. Then I'll stop.\nActually, I'll put all three on bottom if they are all useless. But Gravedigger might be useful to get a big maggot back later. \nNah, I'm at 34 life. I need impact.\nActually, let's just dump the lands.\n\nAction: choose index 2 (Swamp).\nThen choose index 1 (Terramorphic).\nThen answer=true to confirm scry? Or is it automatic?\nUsually scry in this engine: pick cards to bottom, then confirm.\n\nRECRUIT! GET TO THE BOTTOM OF THE DECK! YOU'RE NOT NEEDED!\nIndex 2 (Swamp).",
