      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "MAGGOTS! Timmy is down to 5 life! He's bleeding out! Good! \nVorosh, don't you dare stop! You get +1/+1 counters next turn? No, Vorosh's ability triggers on combat damage! \n\"Whenever Vorosh, the Hunter deals combat damage to a player, you may pay 2G. If you do, put six +1/+1 counters on it.\"\nI have 4 untapped lands. I should have enough! \n\nWait, did it trigger? I don't see the trigger on the stack.\nOh, \"Whenever Vorosh deals combat damage...\". It should trigger now.\nWait, I only have 4 untapped lands. One is Command Tower, one is Forest, one is Swamp, one is Tainted Peak. \nTainted Peak needs a Swamp or Mountain to tap for B/R. I have Swamps.\nSo I have G from Forest. I need 2 more mana. I can tap Command Tower and Tainted Peak.\n\nLet's see if the trigger appears.\nI need to pass priority for the damage to move the turn forward to the trigger?\nDamage has been dealt? Timmy is at 5 life (was 14). 14 - (6+3) = 5. YES.\n\nWait, Vorosh didn't trigger? \nWait, get_game_state showed:\ncombat:[{attackers:[{name:<ctrl46>Vorosh, the Hunter<ctrl46>,power:<ctrl46>6<ctrl46>,toughness:<ctrl46>6<ctrl46>}],blocked:false,defending:<ctrl46>Gem25F Timmy<ctrl46>}...]\nStep: Combat Damage.\nMaybe the trigger happens after I pass priority in the damage step?\nOr maybe I missed it.\nActually, usually the engine puts it on the stack.\nMaybe it asks for the pay later.\n\nI'll pass priority. \nanswer=false.",
