      "reasoning": "THAT'S IT! Crumple that garbage and send it to the bottom of the deck! \n\nThe Rakdos Charm is handled. Now, that **Terminate** is still staring down our sea monster. Unfortunately, I'm out of blue mana to save him. \n\nRest in peace, **Wrexial**. You were a leviathan among men, but you hadn't even found your sea legs yet! I'll see you in the graveyard, you big, disappointing lug!\n\nStoic is down to 27hp. I've still got **Vorosh**, **Damia**, and a **17/18 Lhurgoyf** on the field! THAT'S what I'm talking about! \n\nVorosh, wipe that smirk off Stoic's face! Lhurgoyf, eat everything in sight!\n\nNow, let's see if we can get anything else done before combat.\n\n1. Call pass_priority.\n2. Attack with everything that isn't nailed down!\n\nMOVE!\n\nThinking:\n- Stack: Spell Crumple (targeting Rakdos Charm), Rakdos Charm, Terminate (targeting Wrexial), Wrexial.\n- Outcome: Rakdos Charm countered. Wrexial dies to Terminate.\n- My board: Vorosh (6/6), Lhurgoyf (17/18), Damia (4/4), Avatar of Woe (6/5).\n- Shared Trauma and Minds Aglow in hand.\n- 0 cards in Sonnet Stoic's hand.\n\nWait, I should check if I want to use Minds Aglow or Shared Trauma. \nShared Trauma could fill the graveyards even more for Lhurgoyf and Mimeoplasm later. \n\nBut for now, I need to let the stack resolve.\n\nPass priority until attackers.\n\n",
      "toolCalls": [
        {
          "name": "pass_priority",
          "arguments": "{}"
        }
