      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "WHAT?! Wrexial is still on the board? And Lhurgoyf is in the graveyard? And my mana pool is empty?!\n\nLISTEN UP, YOU MISERABLE EXCUSES FOR CARDS! I don't know who's in charge here, but this battlefield is a mess! Wrexial, YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO BE DEAD! Lhurgoyf, GET BACK UP! \n\nWait... it looks like the stack resolved but the previous `choose_action` results didn't match the state I expected. No matter! We're in the **Declare Attackers** phase now. \n\nI have **Vorosh (6/6)**, **Damia (4/4)**, and **Wrexial (5/8)** ready to move! **Avatar of Woe** is still nursing her wounds (summoning sickness). \n\nStoic has some flyers and blockers, but we have the power! \n\nThinking:\n- Stoic's blockers: Prosper (1/4 tapped), Dream Pillager (4/4 tapped), 2x Thopter (1/1 tapped), Izzet Chemister (1/1 tapped).\nWait, EVERYTHING is tapped on his side except for a bunch of artifacts and Warlock Class.\n- Actually, looking at the state: `tapped: true` for Prosper, Dream Pillager, both Thopters, Izzet Chemister.\n- He has NO blockers?! \n\nATTACK! ALL OF YOU! WIPE THAT POET OFF THE MAP!\n\n1. get_action_choices\n2. Attack with Vorosh.\n3. Attack with Wrexial.\n4. Attack with Damia.\n5. Confirm.\n\nDO IT NOW!\n\n(Wait, I just noticed Wrexial has summoning sickness in the game state. How? I played him this turn? Yes.)\n\nSo Vorosh and Damia are the only ones who can attack. \n\nMOVE OUT!\n\n",
