      "ts": "2026-02-11T01:13:51.228-08:00",
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "ABOUT TIME! REINFORCEMENTS HAVE ARRIVED!\n\nStoic dealt 4 damage to us with something? Or maybe it was Warlock Class? No, I'm at 14hp. 18 -> 14. \nLooking at the state, I don't see any burn in the graveyard. Oh, it must have been the thopters plus something else. Whatever!\n\nIT'S OUR TURN! **DAMIA** IS ON THE FIELD! \nDamia's triggered ability: \"At the beginning of your upkeep, if you have fewer than seven cards in hand, draw cards equal to the difference.\"\n\nI have 3 cards in hand: **Minds Aglow**, **Shared Trauma**, and **Island**.\nI will draw 4 cards! \n\n\"DAMIA! USE YOUR EYES! FIND ME SOME REAL SOLDIERS! I'M TIRED OF COMMANDING THESE SLACKJWS!\"\n\nBut first, **Avatar of Woe** is ready to work! \n\"AVATAR! STOP NAPPING! DESTROY THAT **PROSPER**! WE'RE TIRED OF HIS TOME-BOUND NONSENSE!\"\n\n1. get_action_choices\n2. Activate Avatar of Woe (index 0).\n3. Target: Prosper, Tome-Bound.\n\nWait... Riddlekeeper is also a target. Prosper is more dangerous long-term. \nActually, if I destroy Prosper, Stoic stops getting treasures and cards. \nTarget Prosper.\n\nDO IT!\n\nWait, this is my upkeep. The Damia trigger is likely on the stack already or about to be. I should activate the Avatar now while I have priority.\n\nWait... if I activate Avatar now, I can't use it later in the turn if something better comes along. But Prosper is a high-priority target.\n\n1. get_action_choices\n2. index 0 (Avatar)\n3. Target index (will check in next step)\n\n\"TARGET ACQUIRED! FIRE!\"\n\nWait, I should check the state.\nStoic: 27hp. \nMy hand: Minds Aglow, Shared Trauma, Island.\nDamia trigger should be on the stack.\n\nLet's look at the choice.\n\n",
