      "reasoning": "\"REPORT! WHAT DO WE HAVE HERE?\"\n\nI have **Buried Alive**! \nI have **Shared Trauma**!\nI have **Sign in Blood**!\nI have **Minds Aglow**!\nI have **Simic Signet**!\nAnd a mystery card (Unknown (df87e62c)).\n\n\"BURIED ALIVE? THAT'S MY KIND OF STRATEGY! DIG A HOLE AND THROW THE MAGGOTS IN IT!\"\n\nStrategic Plan:\n1. Play a Land (Island or Forest).\n2. Cast **Buried Alive**. \n   - I need to put the best meat in the yard for Mimeoplasm or just to have them there.\n   - Brawn? (Already in the Yard?). Let's check the graveyard.\n   - Lord of Extinction? \n   - Some fatty?\n3. Cast **Shared Trauma**? \n   - This mills everyone. With Wrexial and Mimeoplasm, that's good for me. \n   - But I have to be careful not to deck myself or give Stoic too much (he has 0 cards).\n4. Cast **Sign in Blood**? \n   - I have 14 life. I can afford 2 more to draw 2 cards.\n5. **Minds Aglow**? \n   - No, don't help the enemy draw cards. Stoic has 0 cards in hand! Keep it that way!\n\nWait, let's look at **Wrexial**. Wrexial can cast an instant or sorcery from an opponent's graveyard when he deals combat damage. \nStoic's graveyard: Riddlekeeper, Prosper, Dream Pillager (Wait, I killed them). \nLet's check Stoic's yard.\n\n\"PRIVATE! GET ME A ROSTER OF THE ENEMY'S FALLEN!\"\n\nAlso, I have **Avatar of Woe**, **Wrexial**, **Damia**, and **Vorosh** on the field. \nStoic has **Riddlekeeper** (1/4 mill when I attack) and two 1/1 Thopters. \nWait, Riddlekeeper says: \"Whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, its controller mills two cards.\"\nI have 4 big attackers. If I attack with all 4, I mill 8",
