      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Alright, soldiers! Listen up! We have the advantage, but we're not going to take any chances. Stoic is sitting on 27 health, but their hand is empty. Prosperity is dead, and the field is mostly ours.\n\nHere's the plan:\n1. **Island** - Play that land. We need the mana to keep our operations running.\n2. **Buried Alive** - This is a precision strike. We're going to dump **Lord of Extinction**, **Wonder**, and **The Mimeoplasm**'s next suit into the graveyard. Wait, I don't see Lord of Extinction or Wonder in my deck list yet... Let's look at what's available. I'll pick the biggest, meanest things I can find. **Terastodon**? **Woodfall Primus**? I'll check the options when I cast it. But for now, let's just get the value.\n3. **Sign in Blood** - Draw more cards. I have 14 life, I can afford 2. I need more options.\n4. **Minds Aglow** and **Shared Trauma**? NO. We are not helping the enemy. We are not milling ourselves into oblivion while that Riddlekeeper is watching.\n\n\"ISLAND! GET ON THE FIELD! NOW!\"\n\n1. get_action_choices\n2. index 2 (Island)\n\nThen we'll see where we are.\n\nWait, I should check my graveyard again. **Brawn** is already there. So my creatures have Trample. \n**Wrexial** and **Vorosh** are going to have a field day.\n\n\"MOVING OUT!\"\n\nfyi: Buried Alive targets. I should see what's in my library. \nActually, I'll just play the land first.\n\n\"MAGGOTS, ATTENTION!\"\n\n1. get_action_choices\n2. index 2 (Island)\n\n(Actually, looking at the choices: Island is index 2. Forest is index 6. Buried Alive is index 3. Wait, I'll check again.)\n\nBuried Alive: {2}{B}. \nCurrent mana: 15 untapped lands/rocks. Plenty.\n\nLet's play the Island.\n\n1. choose_action(index=2)\n\nWait, get_action_choices first.\n\n(",
