      "ts": "2026-02-11T01:19:20.561-08:00",
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "\"WHAT?! HE CAST PHITHISIS?! OR FLESHBAG?!\"\n\nWait, let's check the stack or recent actions. \n`Select a creature (to sacrifice)`. \nStoic cast something that makes me sacrifice. \nHe had **Fleshbag Marauder** in my graveyard? No. \nHe had **Danse Macabre** in his graveyard. \nDid he cast it? \n\"Each player sacrifices a creature. You may put a creature card from a graveyard that was sacrificed this way onto the battlefield under your control with a mana value less than or equal to the amount of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\nWait, no. \n\nCheck exile: **Phthisis**. \n\"Destroy target creature. Its controller loses life equal to its power plus its toughness.\"\nWait, that's DESTROY. Not sacrifice. \n\n\"WHY AM I SACRIFICING?! DID HE CAST **HEX**?!\"\nHex is \"Destroy up to six\". \n\nWait... **Fevered Suspicion**! \nHe exiled cards from my deck. \nDid he hit **Fleshbag Marauder**? \nNo, it's in my graveyard. \n\nMaybe he hit **Butcher of Malakir**? \nNo, in my yard. \n\nCheck the game state/action log! \nWait, I can't check the log easily. \n\n\"I DON'T CARE WHO DID IT! WE'RE LOSING A MAN!\"\n\nChoices to sacrifice:\n0. Avatar of Woe\n1. Wrexial\n2. Damia\n3. Vorosh\n\n\"AVATAR! YOU'VE DONE NOTHING ALL DAY BUT NAP! GET OUT THERE AND COVER THE RETREAT!\"\n\nI definitely want to keep Vorosh (attacker), Wrexial (attacker), and Damia (card draw). \nAvatar of Woe is great, but she's tapped and I have plenty of threats. \n\n\"AVATAR! DISMISSED!\"\n\nWait, index 0 is Avatar of Woe. \n\n\"MOVE IT, SOLDIER!\"\n\n1. choose_action(index=0)\n\n(Wait, I should check if there's any reason to keep her. \nShe costs {B}{B} if there are 10+ creatures in yards. \nThere are currently: \nMy yard: 19 cards.",
