      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "\"CONSUMING VAPORS! THAT'S THE CULPRIT!\"\n\nStoic hit **Consuming Vapors** with Fevered Suspicion. \n\"Target player sacrifices a creature. You gain life equal to that creature's toughness. Rebound.\"\nStoic is up to 17 life. \nAvatar of Woe (Toughness 5) gave him 5 life. \n\n\"COWARDLY HEALING! STAND AND FIGHT LIKE A MAN!\"\n\nIt's still Stoic's Precombat Main. \nHe still has 0 cards in hand. \nHe still has 3 treasures. \n\n\"WAITING FOR THE NEXT MOVE! DON'T BLINK!\"\n\nWait, why did the turn counter not go up? \nIt was Turn 13 when I attacked. \nNow it's Turn 13 and Stoic is the active player. \nThe turn hasn't passed to him until after my turn ended. \nSo it's correctly his turn 13. \n\n\"I'M LOSING TRACK OF TIME IN THIS FOXHOLE!\"\n\n1. pass_priority. \n\n(Wait, I should check if he's going to use **Lorcan** or **Apex of Power**. \nHe has 17 life now. \nHe has enough mana for Lorcan (7). \nLorcan is in exile. \nHe can cast it because Prosper exiled it. \n\n\"STAY SHARP! LORCAN IS COMING!\"\n\n1. pass_priority.\n\nTarget player for Consuming Vapors was Gem3F Sarge. \nHe also gets a 2/2 Beholder from Fevered Suspicion.\n\n\"WHERE'S THE BEHOLDER? I DON'T SEE THE EYE-BALL MONSTER!\"\n\nWait, `battlefield` for Stoic: \n\"Thopter Token\" (x2), \"Izzet Chemister\", \"Riddlekeeper\". \nNo Beholder yet? \nAh, Fevered Suspicion: \"For each spell cast this way, create a 2/2 black Beholder creature token.\"\nHe cast Vow of Malice and Consuming Vapors. \nHe should have 2 Beholders. \n\n\"SHOW ME YOUR PERMIT FOR THOSE EYE-BALLS!\"\n\nWait, they aren't in the list? ",
