      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "\"SZADEK IS ON THE STACK! I REPEAT, SZADEK IS ON THE STACK!\"\n\nWait, where did the mana come from? \nI had 5 mana floating. \nI tapped Tainted Peak for {B}. \nThat's 6. \nWhere's the 7th?! \nAh, did I tap another land? \nThe state shows many lands tapped now. \nIt says `mana_pool: {C:2, G:1, U:2}`. \nWait, if Szadek costs 7 and is on the stack, the mana should be gone. \n\n\"I DON'T QUESTION ARTILLERY WHEN IT'S ON THE WAY!\"\n\nWait, Szadek costs {3}{U}{U}{B}{B}. \nMy pool was {C:2, G:1, U:2}. That's 5. \nI needed {B}{B} plus one more generic (or just two black). \nMaybe the game took the mana and Szadek is waiting for resolution. \n\n\"ALL UNITS, STAND BY! SZADEK INBOUND!\"\n\n1. pass_priority. \n\n(Wait, I still have lands to play). \nI have **Svogthos, the Restless Tomb** in hand. \nAnd two Forests. \nI can't play them until Szadek resolves or is countered. \n\n\"HUP-TWO!\"\n\n1. pass_priority. \n\n(Wait, I'll check if I should attack now). \nStoic has **Lorcan** (6/6). \nHe has two **Thopters** (1/1). \nHe has **Riddlekeeper** (1/4). \nHe has **Izzet Chemister** (1/3). \nWarlock Class (Level 1). \n\nIf I attack with **Vorosh** (6/6), **Wrexial** (5/8), and **Damia** (4/4)... \nHe blocks Vorosh with Lorcan? \nVorosh dies? \nGrave Pact triggers! Stoic sacrifices a creature! \n\n\"EXCELLENT! VOROSH, YOU'RE THE BAIT! TAKE THAT DEMON DOWN WITH YOU!\"\n\nWait, Vorosh has Flying. Lorcan has Flying. \nThey bounce. \n",
