      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "\"IMPACT! VOROSH AND WREXIAL HAVE STRUCK! NOW FOR THE AFTERMATH!\"\n\nSonnet Stoic is at 8 life. \n(17 - 5 from Wrexial - 4 from Damia = 8). \nWait, Vorosh hasn't put his counters on yet? Or maybe he hit? \nDamia hit. \nVorosh hit. \nWrexial hit. \n\nWait, Stoic's life went from 17 to 8. That's 9 damage. \nWrexial (5) + Damia (4) = 9. \nWhere is Vorosh? \nVorosh is a 6/6 flyer. \n\nAh, Vorosh and Wrexial both have triggers. \nVorosh: \"Whenever Vorosh deals combat damage to a player, you may pay {2}{G}. If you do, put six +1/+1 counters on it.\"\nWrexial: \"Whenever Wrexial deals combat damage to a player, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from that player's graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into a graveyard this turn, exile it instead.\"\n\nI need to pick which one goes on the stack FIRST (meaning the second one resolves first). \n\n\"VOROSH! YOU'RE LOOKING HUNGRY! WREXIAL! FIND ME A POEM I CAN BURN!\"\n\nLet's look at Stoic's graveyard for Wrexial targets:\n**Fevered Suspicion** (MV 8) - \"Each opponent exiles cards from the top of their library until they exile a nonland card... cast those cards without paying their mana costs.\" \n**Hex** - \"Destroy six target creatures.\"\n**Commune with Lava** - Exile cards, play them. \n**Bituminous Blast** - Damage + Cascade. \n**Terminate** - Destroy. \n**Danse Macabre** - Sacrifice + Return. \n\n\"FEVERED SUSPICION! I'LL TAKE THAT!\"\n\nI'll put Vorosh's trigger on the stack first, then Wrexial's, so I can cast the spell and then see if I want to pay for Vorosh's counters. \nActually, I don't have {2}{G} for Vorosh anyway. All my lands are tapped except",
