    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Halimar Depths before Dimir Aqueduct is poor land sequencing. With no lands on the battlefield, this is the perfect time to play Dimir Aqueduct (enters tapped with no land to bounce back). Next turn, Haiku Villain will likely play Dimir Aqueduct and be forced to bounce Halimar Depths back to hand, losing a turn of land development. Playing Aqueduct now means turn 3 could have Swamp untapped + Aqueduct for 3 mana (UBB), enabling Loyal Subordinate or Dimir Signet.",
