    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sonnet Stoic cast Danse Macabre without first playing a land from hand. They had Swamp and Mountain available to play. Playing Swamp first would have provided the second black mana needed, saving the Treasure token that was sacrificed to help pay for the spell. The Treasure token represents future mana flexibility that was needlessly spent.",
