    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Fleecemane Lion before combat is suboptimal when holding Angelic Gift (which could be used as a combat trick to grant flying and draw a card) and Valorous Stance (indestructible or removal). By casting the creature pre-combat, Timmy reveals information unnecessarily and loses the option to hold up mana for tricks. Additionally, Lumbering Falls could have been activated as a 3/3 attacker this turn, and casting the Lion pre-combat means less mana available for other plays. More importantly, if Timmy wanted to equip Sword of Hours to a creature and attack, playing the Lion post-combat would have been equivalent since it has summoning sickness anyway - but the mana spent now can't be used for Valorous Stance if needed during combat.",
