    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Valorous Stance during precombat main phase without an immediate threat to respond to. Valorous Stance is an instant-speed combat trick or removal spell that is almost always better held up as a reactive play. Using it proactively here means either destroying a creature preemptively (when it could be saved for a more critical threat) or granting indestructible to nothing meaningful. Additionally, casting spells before combat when holding Angelic Gift (which could be a combat trick giving flying + drawing a card) and with Sword of Hours on board suggests poor sequencing - Fleecemane Lion should likely be cast first, then equipment attached, then consider combat before using removal/protection spells.",
